  "id": "Compound::DB01124 - Disease::DOID:9352",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset strongly suggests a relationship between Tolbutamide and Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, supported by its inclusion in the Sulfonylurea Compounds class. This class is associated with antidiabetic agents that regulate blood glucose levels by stimulating insulin secretion. The evidence is corroborated by multiple paths, each linking Tolbutamide to specific sulfonylurea compounds such as Chlorpropamide, Glipizide, and Glyburide, all of which are known to treat Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. The lowest common ancestors of these compounds, including Sulfonylurea Antidiabetic Agents and N-Sulfonylureas, further reinforce the classification and functional role of Tolbutamide within this class. The high final score of 0.8641 indicates a strong and consistent relationship across the network, highlighting the importance of sulfonylurea compounds in the pathogenesis of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. The evidence suggests that Tolbutamide, through its classification as a sulfonylurea antidiabetic agent, may contribute to the management of this condition, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
